      <div type="clause" n="67">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 67</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="67" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="118" ed="#liebermann"/>CXI. Gif mon geþingað<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Ine_67.lnote.oe.16"/> gyrde landes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_67.lnote.oe.10-2"/> oþþe mare<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Ine_67.lnote.oe.17"/> to rædegafole ⁊ geereð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Ine_67.lnote.oe.18"/>, gif se hlaford him wile<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Ine_67.lnote.oe.19"/> þæt land<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_67.lnote.oe.10-2"/> aræran to weorce<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Ine_67.lnote.oe.20"/> ⁊ to gafole, ne þearf he him onfón, gif he him nan botl<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Ine_67.lnote.oe.21"/> ne selð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Ine_67.lnote.oe.22"/>, ⁊ þolie þara<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Ine_67.lnote.oe.23"/> æcra.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="67" corresp="#wit-ot-frags"><pb n="118" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_67.lnote.oe.1-2"/> mon ...ngað gyrde londes oþ ... gafole ..., gif se hlaford hi...ran to weorce ⁊ ..gafole, ne þearf ...</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="67" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="118" ed="#liebermann"/>CXI. Gif mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_67.lnote.oe.1-3"/> gyrde londes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_67.lnote.oe.1-3"/> geþingeð oþþe mare to rædegafole ⁊ ereð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_67.lnote.oe.4"/>, gif se hlaford him wile ðæt lond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_67.lnote.oe.1-3"/> aræran to weorce ⁊ to gafole, ne þearf he him onfon gif he him nan botl ne slihð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_67.lnote.oe.5"/>, ⁊ þolige his æcera.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="67" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="119" ed="#liebermann"/>Be gyrde. Gyf mon geðingað gyrde landes oððe mare to rædegafole ⁊ geerað, gyf se hlaford him wyle þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> land aræran to weorce ⁊ to gafole, ne ðearf he him onfon, gyf he him nan botl ne sylþ, ⁊ ðolie ðara acera.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_67.lnote.oe.1"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="67" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="119" ed="#liebermann"/>Si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_67.lnote.oe.7"/> quis componat pro uirgata terre uel amplius ad<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_67.lnote.oe.8"/> gablum et arabit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_67.lnote.oe.9"/>, si dominus uelit ei terram illam ponere ad gablum et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_67.lnote.oe.10"/> opus, non necesse est hoc excipi, si nulla domus commissa sit ei, sed<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_67.lnote.oe.11"/> perdat ipsas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Ine_67.lnote.oe.12"/> acras.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="58" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be gyrde.] Gif mon geþingað gyrde landes oþþe mare to rædegafole ⁊ geereð<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#Ine_67.attnote.fn.5"/>, gif se hlaford him wile þæt land aræran to weorce ⁊ to gafole, ne þearf he him onfón, gif he him nan botl ne selð<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#Ine_67.attnote.fn.6"/>, ⁊ þolie þara<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#Ine_67.attnote.fn.7"/> æcra.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="68" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="428" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{CXI} Gif mon geþingað gyrde landes oþþe mare to rædegafole ⁊ geereð: gif se hlaford him wile þæt land aræran to weorc ⁊ to gefole, ne þearf he him onfón gif he him nan botl ne selð; ⁊ þolie þara æcra.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="119" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_67.lnote.de.1"/> jemand eine Gerte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_67.lnote.de.2"/> Landes oder mehr auf Vertragsabgabe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_67.lnote.de.3"/> pachtet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_67.lnote.de.4"/> und beackert, [später jedoch] der [Grund]herr ihm das Land auf Frondienst<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_67.lnote.de.5"/>, ausser auf Pachtzins, steigern<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_67.lnote.de.6"/> will, so braucht der [Bauer] es nicht anzunehmen, wenn jener [Herr] ihm nicht [auch] eine Hofstätte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_67.lnote.de.7"/> giebt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_67.lnote.de.8"/>, und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_67.lnote.de.9"/> entbehre der Äcker.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone leases a yardland or more at a fixed rent and ploughs it, [but later] the [land]lord wishes to raise the land [to require] labour-service as well as rent, then the [peasant] need not accept it, if that [lord] does not [also] give him a dwelling, and let him forgo the fields.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="59" ed="#attenborough"/>If a man takes a yard<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_67.attnote.n.1"/> of land or more, at a fixed rent, and ploughs it, [and] if the lord requires service as well as rent, he [the tenant] need not take the land if the lord does not give him a dwelling; but [in that case] he must forfeit the crops<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Ine_67.attnote.n.2"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="407" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone covenants for a yardland or more at a fixed rent, and ploughs it, if the lord wishes to increase for him the [rent of the] land by demanding service as well as rent, he need not accept it, if he does not give him a dwelling; and he is to forfeit the crops.<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#Ine_67.whinote.n.3"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="429" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone takes on a fourth part of a hide or more at fixed rent and ploughs it: if the lord [later] wishes to raise the land [in terms of value] in regard to work and to rent, he need not accept this if he [the lord] does not give him a dwelling, and he [the lord] must forfeit the crops.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">119</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">118</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> Gif</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to Gif</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">119</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">i <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">i R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">119</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ad g. <hi rend="italic">fehlt M Hk Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ad g. lacking in M Hk Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">119</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">arauerit <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">arauerit Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">119</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">uel <hi rend="italic">Lond; darüber</hi> ad <hi rend="italic">Co</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">uel Lond; above it ad Co</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">119</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Lond;</hi> nec <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Lond; nec the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">119</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">illas <hi rend="italic">Lond;</hi> a. i. <hi rend="italic">M Hk Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">illas Lond; a. i. M Hk Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.oe.1-3" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">118</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">118</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">davor zwei Buchstaben radirt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">two letters erased before it</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">118</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">118</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-geð gyrd <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-geð gyrd So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.oe.10-2" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">118</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">lon. <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lon. So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">118</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">mære <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">mære Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">118</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ræþ <hi rend="italic">Ld; darüber</hi> hereð <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ræþ Ld; above it hereð So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">118</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">wille <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wille So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">118</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">weorc <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">weorc So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">118</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">botle <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">botle So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">118</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sylþ, ⁊ ne ðolige <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sylþ, ⁊ ne ðolige Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">118</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þæra <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þæra So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">80</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ine wünschte wohl 68 auf 66 folgen zu lassen. Doch behandelt auch 67 kündbares <hi rend="italic">læn</hi> gegen Leistung des Landnehmers. — Nicht etwa Neubruch (Rodung) folgt aus <hi rend="italic">geereð,</hi> wie Williams in <hi rend="italic">Archaeologia</hi> 33 (1849) 273 meint</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Ine probably wished 68 to follow 66. Yet 67 too deals with revocable <hi rend="italic">læn</hi> in return for services by the tenant. — It does not follow from <hi rend="italic">geereð</hi> that new breaking (clearing) is meant, as Williams in <hi rend="italic">Archaeologia</hi> 33 (1849) 273 thinks</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">80</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Hufe 6; Bauer 5. 10</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Hufe 6; Bauer 5. 10</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">80</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘auf bereite, in Geld oder Naturalien zahlbare, Abgabe’; ahd. <hi rend="italic">bereit</hi> (dän. <hi rend="italic">reede,</hi> an. <hi rend="italic">reiðu</hi>) heisst ‘bar’. <hi rend="italic">Gafol</hi> 2 Zeilen weiter ist synonym, der Ggs. ‘Fron’. Das Wort hat nichts mit <hi rend="italic">ræd</hi> ‘Rat’ oder <hi rend="italic">rad</hi> ‘Ritt’ zu tun. Das Adj. <hi rend="italic">rædegafollic</hi> wird <hi rend="italic">fiscalis</hi> glossiert</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘for a ready rent, payable in money or in kind’; OHG <hi rend="italic">bereit</hi> (Dan. <hi rend="italic">reede,</hi> ON <hi rend="italic">reiðu</hi>) means ‘cash’. <hi rend="italic">Gafol</hi> 2 lines further on is synonymous; the contrast is ‘labour service’. The word has nothing to do with <hi rend="italic">ræd</hi> ‘counsel’ or <hi rend="italic">rad</hi> ‘riding’. The adj. <hi rend="italic">rædegafollic</hi> is glossed <hi rend="italic">fiscalis</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">80</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl.</hi> Urk.: Land vom Kloster erlangen <hi rend="italic">to rihtan gafole, swaswa hyt geþingian magan;</hi> Bi 486</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf.</hi> charter: to obtain land from the monastery <hi rend="italic">to rihtan gafole, swaswa hyt geþingian magan;</hi> Bi 486</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">80</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Opera</hi> und <hi rend="italic">census</hi> heissen die beiden bäuerlichen Leistungsarten allgemein; Nasse <hi rend="italic">Feldgemein.</hi> 51. <hi rend="italic">Weorcwyrðe</hi> bed. ‘fronpflichtig’ bei M. Förster in Morsbach <hi rend="italic">Festschr.</hi> 178</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Opera</hi> and <hi rend="italic">census</hi> are the general names for the two kinds of peasant dues; Nasse <hi rend="italic">Feldgemein.</hi> 51. <hi rend="italic">Weorcwyrðe</hi> means ‘liable to labour service’ in M. Förster in Morsbach <hi rend="italic">Festschr.</hi> 178</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">80</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nicht ‘reichen’. — Da Fron zur Pacht noch im 13. Jh. zugefügt ward (<hi rend="italic">Domesday of St. Paul’s</hi> ed. Hale 23), so versprach ein Chartular, dass die Villanen Rochesters <hi rend="italic">dominus non ponet</hi> (wie hier Q) <hi rend="italic">ad operam sine consensu eorundem;</hi> Vinogradoff in <hi rend="italic">Law Quart. Rev.</hi> 1888 p. 268</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">not ‘to hand over’. — Since labour service was still being added to rent in the 13th cent. (<hi rend="italic">Domesday of St. Paul’s</hi> ed. Hale 23), a cartulary promised that, as to the villeins of Rochester, <hi rend="italic">dominus non ponet</hi> (as Q here) <hi rend="italic">ad operam sine consensu eorundem;</hi> Vinogradoff in <hi rend="italic">Law Quart. Rev.</hi> 1888 p. 268</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.de.7" n="7" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">80</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Also nicht notwendig folgte aus der Übernahme des kleinen Ackerguts, wohl aber aus der eines Hofes im abhängigen Dorf, die Fron für das Herrschaftsgut</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Thus labour service on the demesne did not necessarily follow from taking over the small arable holding, but it did follow from taking over a homestead in the dependent village</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.de.8" n="8" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">80</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘aufschlägt’ H, sonst vom Zelt gesagt, <hi rend="italic">s. Wb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘pitches’ H, otherwise said of a tent; see <hi rend="italic">Wb</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_67.lnote.de.9" n="9" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">80</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">H’s ‘seine’ ändert den Sinn nicht. — Nicht ‘Grundherr verliere die Ernte’, denn <hi rend="italic">æcer</hi> heisst ‘Saatflur’, <hi rend="italic">seges</hi>, nicht ‘Korn’. — Nur Ld Q <hi rend="smallcaps">ii</hi> (danach Thorpe, Schmid) verneinen den Landverlust des Zinsmannes: das ist wohl eines Klerikers bauerfreundliche Einschiebung. Kemble (<hi rend="italic">Saxons</hi> I 310), angeregt von 68, kombiniert Price und Thorpe: der Bauer ‘soll die von ihm gesäte Ernte nicht verlieren’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">H’s ‘his’ does not change the sense. — Not ‘the landlord shall lose the crop’, for <hi rend="italic">æcer</hi> means ‘sown land’, <hi rend="italic">seges</hi>, not ‘corn’. — Only Ld Q <hi rend="smallcaps">ii</hi> (and, following them, Thorpe and Schmid) deny that the rent-payer loses the land: this is probably a cleric’s peasant-friendly interpolation. Kemble (<hi rend="italic">Saxons</hi> I 310), prompted by 68, combines Price and Thorpe: the peasant ‘shall not lose the crop sown by him’</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_67.attnote.fn.5" n="5" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><label>geereð</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ereð</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_67.attnote.fn.6" n="6" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><label>selð</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">slihð</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_67.attnote.fn.7" n="7" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><label>þara</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">his</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_67.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">192</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The <hi rend="italic">gyrd</hi> (‘virgate’) was no doubt, as in later times, a quarter of a ploughland. It is more or less the normal holding of the <hi rend="italic">villanus</hi> in Domesday Book (see Maitland, <hi rend="italic">Domesday Book and Beyond</hi>, p. 36 ff.). It is not clear that the hide was identified with the ploughland in the time of Ine.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_67.attnote.n.2" n="2" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">192</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Thorpe and Kemble (<hi rend="italic">Saxons in England</hi>, <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi>. p. 310) understand this to mean that the tenant shall not be deprived of the results of his labour. Liebermann translates ‘so braucht der [Bauer] es nicht anzunehmen wenn jener [Herr] ihm nicht [auch] eine Hofstätte giebt, und entbehre der Äcker.’ He says <hi rend="italic">æcer</hi> means not ‘korn’ but ‘saatflur’; but see <hi rend="italic">æcer</hi>, B. and T. Suppl.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Ine_67.whinote.n.3" n="3" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">407</biblScope></bibl><label>crops</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">I assume that the situation considered is when the original agreement has expired, and the lord will not renew it on the old terms.</seg></note>
      </div>
